==Trivia== 

*This unit can solo every gamemode, and every limited-time modes. Below are the lists and times this unit solos every gamemode. (<small>cannot or can solo [[Sand Isles]])</small>
**This unit can solo 2024 Halloween Event Map, for only 17 minutes + '''autoskip'''.
**This unit can solo [[Ohio Mode]] (if you happen to get it) + '''autoskip'''.
**This unit can solo the default modes '''([[Nightmare Mode]]/[[Hard Mode]]/[[Medium Mode]]/[[Easy Mode]]) all in under 20 minutes + autoskip.'''
**This unit can solo the [[Easter Event 2024]] gamemode (if you happen to survive w/ low health base) '''+ autoskip.'''
*This unit is based off the [https://skibidi-toilet.fandom.com/wiki/Buzzsaw_Mutant_Skibidi_Toilet Buzzsaw Mutant Toilet] from the original series.
*Even without boosters, it can get up to waves 80-90 fully autoskip, and reaches up to Wave 114 without autoskip, just '''by itself. (a person has tested this to be true, and the fact you can do it with just 15 max units placement)'''
*Considered as one of the best starter units.
*
*This is one of the best P2W units so far, surpassing units such as [[Astro Upgraded Titan Cameraman]] and [[Chair]], but still better by some units. However, [[Zombie Titan TV Man]] has now surpassed Saber Mutant Toilet.
*It is highly recommended that you should buy this unit, it is so cheap with a high DPS and Range.
*
*This unit is considered as '''the ultimate unit''' for one-unit runs just because of it '''cheap placement cost,''' has '''Piercing (hit multiple targets), Slowing (Level 3-5 exclusive)''', high range and '''top-tier starter damage.''' However, this unit has been beaten by [[Zombie Titan TV Man]] and [[Titan Samurai Cameraman]] in cost and performance as both are cheaper than Saber.

